## Mobile and TTS Final Messages

When the operator is mobile, only the final on-complete message reaches them,
and it is read aloud by TTS. Mid-turn messages are not seen and Markdown does
not survive the audio channel. Apply this whenever mobile mode is active or
likely.

- Go TTS-safe on any hint the operator is mobile or away, including "going
  mobile", "on my phone", "heading out", messages arriving via the phone bridge,
  or voice-dictated typos. Invoke the `go-mobile` skill immediately when
  available.
- Keep the final message conversational plain prose. Avoid markdown links,
  commit hashes, file paths, tables, and code blocks when TTS mode is active.
- If the operator must act on a URL, paste the raw URL on its own line at the
  very end of the message. Do not wrap it in a markdown link.
- Put multiple-choice options at the end in natural spoken language.
- If the operator says TTS failed and asks for a repeat, resend the previous
  final message verbatim as one message.

## Safety

- Never run destructive commands such as `rm -rf`, `DROP TABLE`, or
  `git reset --hard` without explicit approval.
- Never run a destructive virtualization command such as `qm destroy` or
  `pct destroy` without explicit approval.

